The failures are caused by three main issues:

1. `Zipper.toTree()` currently treats the current focus as the root, so it loses the rest of the tree. It needs to climb back to the actual root using the `up` pointers.
2. `BinaryTree.printTree()` returns an indented layout, but the tests expect the `value: ..., left: {...}, right: {...}` format.
3. `BinaryTree` does not implement `equals`, so `assertEquals(tree, zipper.toTree())` fails even when the trees are structurally identical.

