board[r][c]='.';`. Simpler no Arrays.

Then `connects`:
```
private boolean connects(char player, boolean vertical) {
 if (rows == 0 || cols == 0) return false;
 boolean[][] visited = new boolean[rows][cols];
 Queue<int[]> queue = new ArrayDeque<>();
 if (vertical) {
   for c 0..cols-1 if board[0][c]==player ...
 } else {
   for r 0..rows-1 if board[r][0]==player ...
 }
 while ... if (vertical ? r == rows-1 : c == cols-1) return true;
 neighbors bounds nr<rows, nc<cols.
