Need if amount >0 full netting.
Full netting code:
double x = lender.getOwes(borrowerName);
double y = borrower.getOwes(lenderName);
double net = normalize(y + amount - x);
if (net > 0.0) {
    borrower.setOwes(lenderName, net);
    lender.setOwedBy(borrowerName, net);
    lender.setOwes(borrowerName, 0.0);
    borrower.setOwedBy(lenderName, 0.0);
} else if (net < 0.0) {
    double debt = -net;
    lender.setOwes(borrowerName, debt);
    borrower.setOwedBy(lenderName, debt);
    borrower.setOwes(lenderName, 0.0);
    lender.setOwedBy(borrowerName, 0.0);
} else {
    lender.setOwes(borrowerName, 0.0);
    borrower.setOwedBy(lenderName, 0.0);
    borrower.setOwes(lenderName, 0.0);
    lender.setOwedBy(borrowerName, 0.0);
}
Need order of set/remove doesn't matter. But if net >0, borrower.setOwes(lender, net) replaces y. lender.setOwedBy(borrower, net) replaces y. 
lender.setOwes(borrower,0) removes x. borrower.setOwedBy(lender,0) removes x.
If net <0, lender.setOwes(borrower, debt) replaces x. borrower.setOwedBy(lender, debt) replaces x. borrower.setOwes(lender,0) removes y. lender.setOwedBy(borrower,0) 
removes y.
