Flood fill helper:
```
private Set<Point> floodFill(int startX, int startY, boolean[][] visited) {
    Set<Point> region = new HashSet<>();
    if (!inBounds(startX, startY) || !isEmpty(startX, startY) || visited[startY][startX]) {
        return region;
    }
    ArrayDeque<Point> queue = new ArrayDeque<>();
    queue.add(new Point(startX, startY));
    visited[startY][startX] = true;
    int[] dx = {1, -1, 0, 0};
    int[] dy = {0, 0, 1, -1};
    while (!queue.isEmpty()) {
        Point p = queue.poll();
        region.add(p);
        for (int i=0; i<4; i++) {
            int nx = p.x + dx[i];
            int ny = p.y + dy[i];
            if (inBounds(nx, ny) && !visited[ny][nx] && isEmpty(nx, ny)) {
                visited[ny][nx] = true;
                queue.add(new Point(nx, ny));
            }
        }
    }
    return region;
}
```
